      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SAXON KELTON (1) finds it hard to break through. Finished second (24.15) at this track last time making it three minors on end. Has never missed the frame here at the trip from four starts. Has performed well from this box with a win and four minor placings to his name from eight starts. Ready to find winning form. HARD TO ROCK (8) has some solid form under his belt and proved too strong last time to win by 1.3 lengths at this track in a handy 20.11 beating Charlie's Rose. Comes out of a solid form race last start. One of main contenders. DR. WARREN (7) turned in a plain run last time when eighth at The Meadows over 525m behind Naringal Lad (31.01) in a Grade 5. Should play a prominent role. SKI BOOTS (2) is new to this circuit but cannot be left out.",
